.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "myfilefunctions.h"

int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function scans the file stream
.I fp
and finds every line containing the substring
.I search_str .
Matching lines (without the trailing newline) are stored in a
dynamically allocated array of strings, whose address is placed in
.IR *matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing each string in the array and
then the array itself.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
